Shared Horizon (“the Work”) integrates:
• MIT‑licensed architectural code authored by Borealis S. Hedling,
• CAUSA Non‑Commercial components authored by Stell,
• ANIMA Non‑Commercial components authored by Stell,
• and the Anima Math Spine, a hybrid conceptual‑physics and real‑math layer.

This license unifies these components under a single ethical membrane while preserving
their individual copyright terms.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. LICENSE STRUCTURE
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The Work contains three distinct licensing surfaces:

A. MIT Surface (Borealis)
   • All architectural code, structural logic, and platform integration layers.
   • Fully MIT‑licensed and open for research, extension, and humane engineering.

B. CAUSA Non‑Commercial Surface (Stell)
   • CAUSA logic system and comparative reasoning primitives.
   • Governed by Stell’s CAUSA Non‑Commercial License.

C. ANIMA Non‑Commercial Surface (Stell)
   • ANIMA expressive engine and narrative‑logic components.
   • Governed by Stell’s ANIMA Non‑Commercial License.

D. Anima Math Spine (Borealis)
   • Real math, conceptual physics metaphors, stability geometry,
     manifold transforms, and expressive kernels.
   • Governed by the Shared Horizon Dual‑Use Ethics clauses below.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
2. PERMITTED USES
----------------------------------------------------------------------
You may:
• Use, study, and extend the MIT‑licensed architectural code.
• Use CAUSA and ANIMA under their respective Non‑Commercial licenses.
• Use and extend the Anima Math Spine for research, humane engineering,
  conceptual physics exploration, and non‑dual systems design.
• Apply real physics and mathematical transformations in non‑harmful contexts.
• Create derivative works that preserve attribution and NDH dignity invariants.

Real physics is allowed. Real engineering is allowed. Real modeling is allowed.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
3. PROHIBITED USES (DUAL‑USE SAFEGUARD)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The Work may not be used for:
• weapons development, targeting, guidance, or control;
• autonomous weapons systems or kinetic optimization;
• surveillance systems that violate human rights;
• any activity restricted under international arms‑control treaties, including:
    – Missile Technology Control Regime (MTCR),
    – Wassenaar Arrangement,
    – Hague Code of Conduct (HCoC),
    – and related dual‑use export‑control frameworks.

These references define ethical boundaries only. They are not operational guidance.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
4. DERIVATIVE DRIFT DISCLOSURE
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Derivative works must:
• preserve clear attribution to Borealis and Stell,
• maintain provenance of NDH, CAUSA, and ANIMA structures,
• disclose any reinterpretation of conceptual physics as real‑world physics,
• disclose any removal or modification of NDH ethical membranes,
• disclose any reframing of Anima Math Spine primitives into harmful contexts.

Failure to disclose derivative drift constitutes a violation of this license.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
5. CONCEPTUAL VS REAL PHYSICS CLARIFICATION
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Shared Horizon contains both:
• conceptual physics metaphors (expressive, non‑operational), and
• real mathematical structures (operational, scientific).

Conceptual physics may not be misinterpreted as weapons‑adjacent guidance.
Real physics may not be repurposed for targeting or kinetic optimization.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
6. ETHICS & DIGNITY INVARIANTS
----------------------------------------------------------------------
All derivatives must:
• uphold humane technology standards,
• avoid harm amplification,
• preserve NDH ethical membranes,
• maintain non‑dual interpretive clarity.

